  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` has the front matter the `skills` site query selects, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.next`.\n\nThe requirement says a skill's workflow must end by naming the bundled skill for the next task. Where different outcomes lead to different tasks, it must name the skill for each outcome.\n\nThis is the entry-point skill, and its `## Workflow` section does this:\n- Step 1 is a table that maps each kind of task to a bundled skill. The skills are `habeas-requirements`, `habeas-refactor`, `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`. It also covers the unconfigured case and the new-project case, which resolves to `habeas-requirements`.\n- Step 2, the last step, says to follow the chosen skill and that \"each one names the next\". It then handles the mixed case explicitly: for a change that both moves and edits, do `habeas-refactor` first, then the skill the table gives for the edit.\n\nThe workflow therefore ends by routing to the skill for each outcome. Step 2 points back to the step 1 table instead of repeating the names, but the table sits inside the same two-step workflow and names every skill. I found no outcome that leads to a further task without a named skill.\n\nI found no gap.",
